or shifts per accepted edge/threshold; intersect approximate coast-masked OSW display polygons.","method_source_id":"source:814dda03fd8926bd","method_status":"described","object_id":null,"observation_time":"2021-03-07","predicate":"dated_figure_ssh_footprint_candidate","review_date":null,"review_fingerprint":"411af6a0c67f3ad3876d5bf0faa2fd4c4719bedb157cfe38d1c28c0cd93131e0","review_note":null,"review_status":"not_individually_reviewed","reviewer":null,"scope":"Dated instantaneous figure-derived SSH contour proxy during the Ursa shedding event. Attribution to the detached named ring is an editorial interpretation requiring scientific review. Source prints 0.65 cm with unresolved unit; no numerical SSH contour was reconstructed. Not a verified whole-ring physical footprint, material coherent core, 3-D volume, lifetime extent or NASA individual identity. Tested scenarios omit source field error, unknown datum/projection, instrument-dot artifacts and OSW boundary uncertainty; no statistical confidence or physical uncertainty bound follows.","source_date":"2022-12-22","source_id":"source:905e5cc303aaceab","source_locator":"Figure 3, 2021-03-07 (row 3 column 4); Section 2 final paragraph; Section 3.2 temporary-detachment narrative","source_locator_status":"specific","source_snapshot_id":"source:814dda03fd8926bd","subject_id":"eddy:published:ursa-2021","support_claim_id":null,"target_collection":"named_eddy_footprint_candidates","target_id":"footprint_candidate:ursa:2021-03-07","unit":null,"value":null},{"assertion_status":"navigation_only_no_event_identity","evidence_class":"atlas_geometry","id":"claim:footprint_movie_context:footprint_candidate:kraken:2013-05-29:level2_B_3","method":"OSW longitude/latitude polygon-to-crop rectangle intersection, with periodic longitude copies; fractions use angular display area. Prefer a nominally complete crop at highest zoom, then smallest wrapped center-distance score and tile ID.","method_source_id":"source:354f29686c861726","method_