bs_ACC.pdf","source_snapshot_id":"source:2e1077cf29d52f00","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dsr2.2015.12.016","spatial_basis":"The paper identifies mooring arrays in Shelikof Sea Valley for the 1989 transport calculation. This is published local coastal-current evidence; no array endpoints, station coordinates, observed current axis, or footprint are digitized here.","state_assignment_method":"source_reported_gulf_of_alaska_shelikof_locality_to_osw_alsk_semantic_state","state_boundary_limit":"ALSK is assigned by the source-reported northern Gulf of Alaska locality. This is a semantic regional association, not an observed-geometry intersection with the approximate OSW polygon; no BERS association follows from this observation.","state_id":"state:ALSK","time_detail":"Published Table 1 caption explicitly identifies 10 May-15 July 1989 as a sea-valley transport interval. The dates delimit this local calculation, not the full 1984-2014 study window or continuous coverage of the entire coastal system."},{"claim_id":"claim:current_source_observation:0008","entity_id":"current:kuroshio","geometry_status":"source_reported_instrument_points_not_current_axis_or_footprint","id":"current_source_observation:0008","observation_depth_note":"The source reports combined profiles spanning roughly 900 m, with the upper 50 m excluded; the downward ADCP at 123 degrees east malfunctioned. Deeper Luzon Undercurrent flow is distinct from the upper Kuroshio.","observation_end":"2020-05","observation_event_id":"luzon-18n-2018-2020-kuroshio","observation_start":"2018-01","observation_time_precision":"month","observation_type":"paired_upward_and_downward_adcp_moorings","physical_relation":"observed_local_instrument_points_only_whole_current_passage_unresolved","reported_locality":"Three moorings east of Luzon at 18 degrees north, 122.7, 123.0 and 123.3 degrees east","reported_observation_points_lon_lat":[[122.7,18],[123.0,18],[123.3,18]],"reported_section_endpoints_lon_lat":null,"source_